{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{artist: Sarah Adams / Lowell Mason}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Traditional}
{key: F}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 338장}
{title_ko: 내 주를 가까이 하게 함은}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 6/4}
{score: nearer-my-god-to-thee.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, nearer to [F]Thee
E'en though it be a [C]cross that raiseth [F]me
Still all my [Bb]song shall be, [F]nearer, my God, to [C]Thee
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, nearer to [F]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Though like the wanderer, the [Bb]sun gone [F]down
Darkness be [C]over me, my rest a [F]stone
Yet in my [Bb]dreams I'd be [F]nearer, my God, to [C]Thee
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, nearer to [F]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]There let the way ap[Bb]pear, steps unto [F]heaven
All that Thou [C]sendest me in mercy [F]given
Angels to [Bb]beckon me [F]nearer, my God, to [C]Thee
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, nearer to [F]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Then, with my waking [Bb]thoughts bright with Thy [F]praise
Out of my [C]stony griefs Bethel I'll [F]raise
So by my [Bb]woes to be [F]nearer, my God, to [C]Thee
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, nearer to [F]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]Or if on joyful [Bb]wing cleaving the [F]sky
Sun, moon, and [C]stars forgot, upward I [F]fly
Still all my [Bb]song shall be, [F]nearer, my God, to [C]Thee
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, nearer to [F]Thee
{end_of_verse}
